# Code owners — who GitHub requests a review from, automatically.
#
# PLACEHOLDER, and deliberately un-mistakable: this checkout has no configured
# git remote, so the maintainer's GitHub handle is not a fact yet. An owner
# GitHub cannot resolve is worse than none — the rule is silently ignored, no
# reviewer is requested, and "Require review from Code Owners" branch
# protection blocks every pull request with an error nobody can act on.
#
# Before the first push to a real remote, run the same grep the packaging
# metadata is gated on and replace every hit:
#
#   grep -rn PLACEHOLDER .github/CODEOWNERS backend/pyproject.toml site/index.html
#
# Last line wins in this file, so the specific rules come after the general one.

* @PLACEHOLDER

# The architecture contract, the release train, and anything that can publish
# or grant permissions. These change rarely and are expensive to get wrong, so
# they get a named owner even when the catch-all already covers them.
/CLAUDE.md                  @PLACEHOLDER
/AGENTS.md                  @PLACEHOLDER
/CHANGELOG.md               @PLACEHOLDER
/CONTRIBUTING.md            @PLACEHOLDER
/SECURITY.md                @PLACEHOLDER
/LICENSE                    @PLACEHOLDER
/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md     @PLACEHOLDER
/.github/                   @PLACEHOLDER
/scripts/                   @PLACEHOLDER
/backend/pyproject.toml     @PLACEHOLDER
/docs/decisions/            @PLACEHOLDER
/docs/stability.md          @PLACEHOLDER
